  Copyright (C) 2026 CARLOS Contributors

  External Tomcat context descriptor for the drugref2 webapp, baked into the
  carlos-drugref image at conf/Catalina/localhost/drugref2.xml by
  Containerfile.drugref. Tomcat prefers an external descriptor over the WAR's
  own META-INF/context.xml and ignores the in-WAR file entirely.

  Why override at all: the in-WAR descriptor guards the app with
    allow="${drugref.allowedRemoteAddresses:127.0.0.1/32,::1/128}"
  but Tomcat's RemoteCIDRValve splits `allow` on commas BEFORE system-property
  substitution runs, so a ${name:a,b} placeholder whose DEFAULT contains a
  comma fails to parse — the upstream carlos devcontainer overrides the valve
  for exactly this reason (see carlos .devcontainer/drugref/drugref2.xml).
  Values are therefore HARDCODED here.

  Loopback-only is exactly the pod's trust model: CARLOS reaches DrugRef over
  the shared pod network namespace at 127.0.0.1:8180, port 8180 is never
  published, and no other client is legitimate. (The devcontainer needs the
  wider RFC1918 list because its containers sit on a bridge network; the pod
  does not.)
-->
<Context>
    <Valve className="org.apache.catalina.valves.RemoteCIDRValve"
           allow="127.0.0.0/8,::1" />
</Context>
